## Approval gates and risk authority
**Mandatory contractual ePHI go-live gates:** Legal must verify an executed BAA, current subprocessor inventory, applicable flow-down terms, and the intended data flow. No business risk acceptance can waive these requirements.

**Additional security assurance gates:** GRC must review the full SOC 2 report, period coverage, exceptions and bridge letter (or approved alternative assurance), and IT must assess dated recovery-test evidence. If either remains unresolved, the vendor cannot receive an unconditional security assurance approval. Any conditional launch recommendation requires documented compensating controls, expiry, monitoring and CISO approval of the remaining security risk; Legal must separately confirm contractual eligibility. A high residual risk requires CISO approval under the risk methodology, and the business owner acknowledges operational impact. As of 2026-10-17, none of these approvals has been granted and ePHI go-live remains blocked.
